WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:03.800
The Beehive Cluster is an open cluster in the constellation Cancer.

00:04.276 --> 00:13.956
One of the nearest open clusters to Earth, it contains a larger population of stars than other nearby bright open clusters holding around 1,000 stars.

00:14.504 --> 00:22.416
Under dark skies, the Beehive Cluster looks like a small nebulous object to the naked eye, and has been known since ancient times.

00:22.968 --> 00:28.548
Classical astronomer Ptolemy described it as a "nebulous mass in the breast of Cancer".

00:29.100 --> 00:32.929
It was among the first objects that Galileo studied with his telescope.
